# NutriPlan configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, or set these in your
# deployment's environment. Every value below is optional: with none of them
# set the app runs on this machine only (`NUTRIPLAN_GATE=local`).
#
# Never commit a filled-in copy of this file. `.gitignore` excludes `.env`,
# `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`.

# ─── Who may reach the app ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# local  (default) only requests addressed to a loopback host pass.
# hosts            only NUTRIPLAN_ALLOWED_HOSTS pass; loopback is not
#                  implicitly trusted. Use behind a reverse proxy that
#                  forwards the public Host header.
# token            only a matching `nutriplan_token` header or cookie passes.
#                  Use for a private share link.
# off              no gate. Only when something else (VPN, proxy auth,
#                  network policy) is the boundary.
#
# Leave empty to infer: ALLOWED_HOSTS implies `hosts`, TOKEN implies `token`.
# An unrecognised value falls back to `local` (fail closed).
# NUTRIPLAN_GATE=hosts

# Comma-separated hostnames, e.g. `nutriplan.example.com` or
# `nutriplan.example.com,*.nutriplan.example.com`. Ports are ignored.
# A leading `*.` matches subdomains, never the bare domain.
# NUTRIPLAN_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Shared secret for `token` mode. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# The token is accepted only as the `nutriplan_token` header or cookie.
# Query-string tokens are rejected: a token in a URL ends up in browser
# history and proxy logs.
# NUTRIPLAN_TOKEN=

# Set to 1 only when a reverse proxy in front of the app overwrites
# `X-Forwarded-Host` with the public hostname. Forwarded headers are
# client-writable; trusting them without a proxy lets a caller claim to be
# `localhost` and walk past the gate.
# NUTRIPLAN_TRUST_PROXY=

# ─── Reverse-proxy integration (read when the app is built) ─────────────────
#
# Extra origins allowed to invoke server actions, and mirrored by the proxy's
# CSRF check. Only needed when the proxy forwards its own upstream host
# (`127.0.0.1:3000`) instead of the public one. Host patterns only: no scheme,
# no path, no bare `*`; a leading `*.` matches subdomains. A non-default port
# is part of the match, so include it (`app.example.com:8443`). Because Next
# bakes config into the build, set this before `npm run build` /
# `docker build`, not only at runtime.
# NUTRIPLAN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Development only: origins allowed to load the dev server (HMR, LAN
# preview). Ignored in a production build.
# NUTRIPLAN_ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=

# ─── Persistent state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Directory for the SQLite database, saved API keys and AI config. Defaults
# to `./data`. In a container, point this at a mounted volume. With
# `output: "standalone"` the process cwd is the build output, so writing to
# the default would put your data inside the image.
#
# Keep this on a local filesystem. SQLite runs in WAL mode; a network share or
# a cloud-synced folder can interleave writes and corrupt the database.
# NUTRIPLAN_DATA_DIR=/data

# Exact database path. Wins over NUTRIPLAN_DATA_DIR. Intended for tests and
# for pointing at a pre-existing database file.
# NUTRIPLAN_DB_PATH=

# ─── AI providers (bring your own key) ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Keys can also be saved from the Settings page, which writes them to
# `$NUTRIPLAN_DATA_DIR/secrets.json` (mode 0600), keyed by `provider@host`.
# For a deployment, prefer these env vars: nothing secret then lives on the
# writable volume. Setting both an env var and the settings value is an error,
# by design.
#
# An env key is used for the provider's fixed endpoint without a host pin. It
# is released to a custom baseUrl only when that host is listed in the matching
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_<PROVIDER>_HOST variable; an unpinned env key fails closed for a
# custom endpoint. Comma-separated, exact host (and port if non-default).
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_GEMINI_KEY=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_OPENAI_KEY=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_ANTHROPIC_KEY=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_KEY=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_GEMINI_HOST=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_OPENAI_HOST=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_ANTHROPIC_HOST=
# NUTRIPLAN_AI_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_HOST=

# A custom AI base URL must be public HTTPS. Set to 1 to allow a private or
# loopback endpoint (Ollama, a LAN gateway). Link-local addresses are never
# allowed, even with this opt-in.
# NUTRIPLAN_ALLOW_PRIVATE_AI_URLS=

# ─── Food data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# USDA FoodData Central key. Without it the app uses `DEMO_KEY`, which is
# rate-limited per IP and will 429 under normal use. A free key:
# https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
# NUTRIPLAN_USDA_KEY=

# ─── Server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run dev` binds 127.0.0.1 explicitly. `next start` and a container honour
# these; keep the gate as the second control when binding wider.
# Requires Node.js 24 or newer (`engines` in package.json).
# PORT=3000
# HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0
# NODE_ENV=production
